          "url": "https://movingimage.org/event/the-french-connection/"
        },
        {
          "text": "Kubrick series",
          "url": "https://movingimage.org/series/kubrick/"
        },
        {
          "text": "Dr. Strangelove",
          "url": "https://movingimage.org/event/dr-strangelove-or-how-i-learned-to-stop-worrying-and-love-the-bomb-2026/"
        },
        {
          "text": "Testament",
          "url": "https://movingimage.org/event/testament-with-lynne-littman-in-person/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "BAM Filming Filmmakers presents films about Akira Kurosawa, Werner Herzog, Jean-Luc Godard, and Jacques Rivette by Chris Marker, Les Blank, and Claire Denis.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Filming Filmmakers",
          "url": "https://www.bam.org/film/2026/filming-filmmakers"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Roxy Cinema A Bill Gunn series presents Losing Ground and a print of The Landlord , while a 16mm cartoon program plays Sunday.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Losing Ground",
          "url": "https://www.roxycinemanewyork.com/screenings/losing-ground-bill-gunn-at-roxy/"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Landlord",
          "url": "https://www.roxycinemanewyork.com/screenings/the-landlord-35mm-bill-gunn-at-roxy/"
        },
        {
          "text": "a 16mm cartoon program",
          "url": "https://www.roxycinemanewyork.com/screenings/16mm-cartoons-raunchy-sexy-risque-qa/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Paris Theater The Insider plays on 35mm this Saturday.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "The Insider",
          "url": "https://www.paristheaternyc.com/film/the-insider-paris"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Museum of Modern Art A Sergei Loznitsa retrospective continues while Sundays with Steven brings the 1961 and 2021 versions of West Side Story .",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Sergei Loznitsa retrospective",
          "url": "https://www.moma.org/calendar/film/5937"
        },
        {
          "text": "Sundays with Steven",
          "url": "https://www.moma.org/calendar/film/5946"
        },
        {
          "text": "1961",
          "url": "https://www.moma.org/calendar/events/11782"
        },
        {
          "text": "2021",
          "url": "https://www.moma.org/calendar/events/11783"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Film Forum A 4K restoration of Zhang Yimou’s Raise the Red Lantern continues; The Court Jester shows on Sunday.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Raise the Red Lantern",
          "url": "https://filmforum.org/film/raise-the-red-lantern"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Court Jester",
          "url": "https://filmforum.org/film/the-court-jester-ffjr-2026"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Anthology Film Archives The collaborations of Mathieu Amalric and John Zorn are highlighted in a new series while films by D.W. Griffith and Ken Jacobs show in Essential Cinema .",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Mathieu Amalric and John Zorn",
          "url": "https://www.anthologyfilmarchives.org/film_screenings/series/62189"
        },
        {
          "text": "Essential Cinema",
          "url": "https://www.anthologyfilmarchives.org/film_screenings/programs/essential-cinema"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "IFC Center Ken Russell’s reconstructed The Devils continues—read (or listen to) our interview with Mark Kermode on it—while The Reflecting Skin , The Wild Bunch , and a print of Cloverfield play late.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "The Devils",
          "url": "https://www.ifccenter.com/films/the-devils/"
        },
        {
          "text": "our interview with Mark Kermode",
          "url": "https://thefilmstage.com/i-cant-quite-believe-its-happening-mark-kermode-on-resurrecting-ken-russells-the-devils/"
        },
